This crate (`symphonia-codec-aptx`) is a pure-Rust aptX and aptX HD decoder. It is licensed under
the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia (see `LICENSE`).

aptX has no public specification. The decoder is ported from FFmpeg's `libavcodec/aptxdec.c`,
`libavcodec/aptx.c` and `libavcodec/aptx.h` (Copyright (C) 2017 Aurelien Jacobs, 2018 Mauro
Gaspari, Supraja Meedinti), which were written from the libopenaptx work of Pali Rohar, and are
distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later. The quantization
tables and the QMF coefficients (`src/tables.rs`) are extracted programmatically from `aptx.c` and
`aptx.h`.
